JOHN’S REQUIREMENTS

1. Separate Application Roles from Record-Level Permissions

Knowledge Base application roles and individual record permissions are two different concepts.

Application-level role:

* Controls access across the entire KB Admin application.
* Example roles may include Reader/Viewer, Editor, Admin.
* Most users should have limited/default access.
* KB Admin should be a high-privilege role and should be assigned only to appropriate users.

Record-level permissions:

* Allow a user to receive additional permissions for a specific Knowledge Base area/entity without making that user a KB application Admin.
* This is the same general concept already used by Goals and Items in TOW.

Example:

* John Sweet can be a Viewer at the KB application level.
* John Sweet can then be assigned Editor/Author/Publisher permissions specifically for the IT Support knowledge area.
* He must NOT need full KB Admin privileges just to manage IT Support content.

